  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Also, you can mix positional and keyword styles of passing arguments, as shown, BUT all the positional arguments must come first:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 52,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "4 + 5 = 9\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# positional argument is first\n",
    "sum_num(4, y=5)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 24,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "ename": "SyntaxError",
     "evalue": "positional argument follows keyword argument (3181729183.py, line 2)",
