    "def sum_num(x,y):\n",
    "    if type(x) is int and type(y) is int: # ensuring argument values are integers\n",
    "        return x+y\n",
    "    else: # what to do if argument values are not integers\n",
    "        return \"Error. One or all values are not integers\"\n",
    "\n",
    "print(sum_num(2,3))\n",
    "print(sum_num('a',2))\n",
    "print(sum_num('a','b'))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Otherwise, if have two return statements within a function, the function will terminate after encountering the first returnstatement. Therefore, it wil not evaluate the other return statements (also known as **dead code**), as shown below:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 74,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
