   "outputs": [],
   "source": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### *Default Parameters*\n",
    "\n",
    "Default parameters are specified when defining a python function, and take the form of `<`name`>`=`<`value`>`, where `<`value`>` is the default value for that parameter. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Default parameters are **defined ony once** when the function is defined (executed ie), and therefore the default value **is not** redefined each time the function is called."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 31,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def sales(item, price, max_discount, min_price=200):\n",
    "    if price < min_price:\n",
    "        price = min_price\n",
    "    if max_discount > 0.10:\n",
    "        max_discount = 10\n",
    "    print(\"The price of\", item, \"is \", price, \"and a maximum discount of\", max_discount, \"% is applicable.\")"
   ]
  },
